/ read0/read1: the line- and byte-level equivalents of load/sink, for
/ anything on disk that isn't tabular data.

lines: read0 "examples/notes.txt"
lines
count lines

/ a byte range: `len` bytes starting at byte `off`
read0["examples/notes.txt"; 6; 4]

/ the same range, as raw bytes
bytes: read1["examples/notes.txt"; 0; 5]
bytes
bytes[0]
